1
00:00:10,839 --> 00:00:12,800
Do you know why I like games?

2
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:16,559
Because real life...

3
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,440
It’s just so boring.

4
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:24,878
The WOG Championship is kicking off today.

5
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:26,518
This year is going to be better than ever.

6
00:00:26,519 --> 00:00:30,639
Because this is the very first time
WOG is being held in Thailand.

7
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:34,879
And most importantly,
the prize pool is eighteen million baht.

8
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,640
Eighteen million baht.

9
00:00:36,799 --> 00:00:38,799
If it were me.

10
00:00:39,679 --> 00:00:42,639
I’d rather open a soapy massage place instead.
Just a small one.

11
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:48,320
As for the winner,
on top of receiving the eighteen million baht prize.

12
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:53,159
Representing the country... and now,
going global! Competing on the world stage.

13
00:00:55,119 --> 00:00:56,599
My hands shake just looking at it.

14
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,519
Honestly, I want to compete...
but I'd rather just watch.

15
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:03,040
And yeah, back to the whole soapy massage thing
I’m seriously thinking about opening one.

16
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:07,799
Alright, for anyone out there
who dreams of competing on the world stage.

17
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:13,878
This is your chance Your chance Your real shot.

18
00:01:13,879 --> 00:01:16,679
Alright then uh, what was it again?
Wait, did a comment just come in?

19
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,480
Tep G’s not gonna show up. Total coward
probably hiding in here and hasn’t come out yet. Hahaha.

20
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,279
Tep G actually replied.

21
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,679
Your dad’s dead. Whoa.

22
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:30,760
The great Tep G actually replied? Tep G?

23
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,718
Wow, even sending blessings to my dad now?

24
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:35,078
How’d they know my dad was already gone?

25
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:36,599
Just seeing it makes my hands shake.

26
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:39,839
Honestly, I really want to see
what Tep G actually looks like.

27
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:43,239
Tep G is a real mystery.

28
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:46,518
Who knows maybe eighteen million
might be enough to make Tep G reveal their face.

29
00:01:46,519 --> 00:01:48,839
If they really win that eighteen million, I mean.

30
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,718
But I really do want to get to know Tep G.

31
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:52,439
I want to rub shoulders with Tep G.

32
00:01:59,439 --> 00:02:00,599
Rapee.

33
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:04,959
Will you take Noppakao as your wife?

34
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,439
- And do you promise to be faithful to her? / - I do.

35
00:02:07,879 --> 00:02:10,158
Will you love and honor each other
for the rest of your lives?

36
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:11,159
Yes, I will.

37
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,599
The rings. Bring the rings.

38
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:23,960
- You’re husband and wife now.
- Yay!

39
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,158
Why did that happen so fast?

40
00:02:26,159 --> 00:02:28,479
- We need to rush over there three minutes / - Shit.

41
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,919
Hooray! Eat as much as you want, everyone.

42
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:36,319
Hooray! Woohoo!

43
00:02:36,919 --> 00:02:39,120
- Where are you going? / - Kao...

44
00:02:40,439 --> 00:02:42,719
- Kao has to take a shit / - Huh?

45
00:02:43,479 --> 00:02:45,159
- He’s gone. / - Hey, where are you...

46
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:58,120
They say your wedding day
is the most important day in a woman’s life.

47
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,400
And look at the state I’m in now.

48
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:26,360
Shit... it really does look exactly the same.

49
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,079
Fuck, that’s sick.

50
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,919
Look, it’s even got hair.

51
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,479
- Damn, that’s huge / - I’m filming, I’m filming.

52
00:03:33,639 --> 00:03:35,319
- Damn, that’s huge / - Whoa.

53
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:42,719
I remember never teaching you to swear.

54
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:51,560
What is that supposed to be a carving of?

55
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:55,599
It’s a cannon, teacher.
Did you think it was something else?

56
00:03:57,439 --> 00:03:58,840
You little brat.

57
00:04:02,319 --> 00:04:03,959
What are you girls carving, anyway?

58
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,680
You know perfectly well what it looks like.

59
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:08,599
And as for the swearing.

60
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:11,719
Your words reflect your breeding,

61
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:13,840
and your manners reflect your upbringing.

62
00:04:15,199 --> 00:04:18,278
What kind of family do you want
people to think you came from?

63
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:21,720
- Family... / - The Saiya family, Teacher.

64
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:25,518
Saiya’s a planet, not a family name. Shit.

65
00:04:25,519 --> 00:04:27,600
Swearing again? I’m gonna smack you.

66
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,560
Our school teaches us to speak
to one another with respect.

67
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,959
Where did you learn to talk like that?

68
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,839
You’ve got no manners.

69
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,600
You’re dead for sure, you little shit.

70
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:50,759
- I’m taking off conduct points. / - Twenty points.

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,360
- Ten points for conduct - Good.

72
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,919
I ran into Tep G’s team yesterday.

73
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,518
Man, they were fucking brutal.

74
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:02,600
Yeah, fuck I was dead
before I even had the chance to spawn.

75
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,319
What the fuck!

76
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,639
Teacher Noppakao.

77
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:11,399
I know you’re pushing me
to take over as principal this year, Mom.

78
00:05:11,639 --> 00:05:13,399
Why are you acting so inappropriately, dear?

79
00:05:13,839 --> 00:05:15,838
You’re doing just fine as principal, Mom.

80
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:18,000
Besides, there are other things I want to do first.

81
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,480
What are these other things you want to do?

82
00:05:22,279 --> 00:05:24,959
Well... I mean, travel.

83
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:28,999
Or maybe I’ll go do something else
something other than teaching.

84
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,480
A job other than teaching.

85
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:38,078
Oh, fine, I won’t do it then, Mom.

86
00:05:38,079 --> 00:05:39,319
I’ll be a teacher.

87
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,920
I’ll be the principal.

88
00:05:41,199 --> 00:05:42,479
Just like Great-Grandma.

89
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,720
Just like you, Mom.

90
00:05:43,879 --> 00:05:44,879
Good.

91
00:05:58,439 --> 00:06:00,519
Do you remember Aunt Lamphueng’s daughter?

92
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,680
I think he’s quite handsome.

93
00:06:08,839 --> 00:06:09,879
Come here.

94
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,758
P’Phat, P’Pee, let Kao play too.

95
00:06:16,759 --> 00:06:19,720
- No.
- Pleeease, P’Pee.

96
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:23,439
- Pee, let her play with you.
- No.

97
00:06:23,879 --> 00:06:26,279
Pleeease, P’Pee.

98
00:06:28,279 --> 00:06:30,240
We can just play by ourselves, right?

99
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:52,959
Kao, are you okay?

100
00:07:03,439 --> 00:07:04,439
Zombie.

101
00:07:08,879 --> 00:07:12,720
Don’t tell me you’re trying
to set me up with P’Rapee.

102
00:07:20,199 --> 00:07:21,199
Shit.

103
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:26,240
WOG is an SPS game that uses gloves

104
00:07:26,399 --> 00:07:29,999
as part of the gameplay.
Though honestly, you can play it with a keyboard too.

105
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,519
But I feel like using the gloves.

106
00:07:32,759 --> 00:07:36,560
It really pulls you into the game
and makes you feel more immersed.

107
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,319
This is exciting. Really exciting.

108
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,958
And another thing

109
00:07:41,959 --> 00:07:44,559
after narrowing it down from a hundred teams

110
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,720
to just twenty-four,

111
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:50,198
this year we’ve got a wildcard.

112
00:07:50,199 --> 00:07:54,560
So what is a wildcard?
It gives new players a chance

113
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:57,480
to become one of those twenty-four teams.

114
00:07:58,639 --> 00:08:01,439
You’ve got to grab this chance.

115
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:06,439
Whoa, you want to see
TT go up against Tep G?

116
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,600
Honestly,

117
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:10,919
I want to see both TT and Tep G too.

118
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,360
Because I still don’t know who they really are.

119
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,680
But the thing about TT is, they’re kind of a lone wolf.

120
00:08:16,839 --> 00:08:19,439
Always playing solo, doing everything solo.

121
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:23,399
Yeah, no idea if they’ll show up to compete,
but they probably will.

122
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:26,879
Shit, what the hell? Every shot landed.

123
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,399
Wooo! Bang, bang, bang! Wooo!

124
00:08:47,919 --> 00:08:48,919
Wait, wait, wait.

125
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
What is it?

126
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,440
Why’s your name so lame?

127
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:58,360
Lame my ass.

128
00:08:58,759 --> 00:09:00,399
My name is cool as hell.

129
00:09:00,559 --> 00:09:02,639
You know Tep G?

130
00:09:02,879 --> 00:09:05,919
Damn, you sound like an old lady.
You sure you’re not a fake?

131
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,999
You’re this old and still gaming?
Just quit already.

132
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,400
Careful, Auntie. Keep playing
and your fingers might lock up.

133
00:09:21,159 --> 00:09:23,479
Woooooo! So, how’s that?

134
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,960
All bark, no bite. Total loser acting tough.

135
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,158
What now, bitch? Don’t come at me.

136
00:09:28,159 --> 00:09:31,039
That’s Tep G, asshole. Goodbye.

137
00:09:31,159 --> 00:09:32,559
Hey, yo.

138
00:09:33,399 --> 00:09:34,918
That was all you, bro. Seriously.

139
00:09:34,919 --> 00:09:36,576
Beating regular players isn’t enough for you now?

140
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,775
Now you’re showing off against kids too.

141
00:09:37,799 --> 00:09:40,255
- Are you roasting me or complimenting me?
- Complimenting you.

142
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:43,240
Kao, I’m telling you,
you should play WOG with me next time.

143
00:09:43,399 --> 00:09:45,558
No way. I’ve only played,
like, two or three games.

144
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:48,480
Dude, don’t you wanna know
who’s been playing in the room I made?

145
00:09:48,639 --> 00:09:49,639
Who?

146
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,159
Housand Thunder.

147
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,678
- P’Tim?
- Who’s that?

148
00:09:52,679 --> 00:09:54,319
- You sure, bro?
- What if it’s a fake account?

149
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,240
No way.

150
00:09:55,241 --> 00:09:57,200
Probably fake, but...

151
00:09:57,519 --> 00:10:00,399
They’ve taken first place
in my room three matches in a row.

152
00:10:00,879 --> 00:10:01,959
So what’s it gonna be? You in?

153
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:04,719
- I’m in, bro.
- He wasn’t asking you. He was asking P’Kao.

154
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,119
Fine. Bring it on.

155
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:08,320
I’m telling you, if we beat them.

156
00:10:08,519 --> 00:10:10,480
We’re gonna blow up. You in?

157
00:10:12,559 --> 00:10:13,959
Thousand Thunder. We’re talking about
a legendary gamer who’s never lost to anyone.

158
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,918
We’re talking about a legendary gamer
who’s never lost to anyone.

159
00:10:16,919 --> 00:10:18,719
And a champion in every game.

160
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:21,799
And by every game, I mean every game.

161
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,320
Kao. Hey, Kao.

162
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,759
Are you in or not? If not, I’m not begging.

163
00:10:28,559 --> 00:10:29,559
I’m in.

164
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:32,079
- You guys ready?
- Ready.

165
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,279
So, what are we eating?

166
00:10:35,519 --> 00:10:36,999
Oh, you’re gaming?

167
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,399
Sorry, sorry. I won’t disturb you.

168
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,479
- Minced pork omelet.
- Not eating. I’m doing IF.

169
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,518
Basil pork with a fried egg, no chili.

170
00:10:41,519 --> 00:10:43,079
Seafood fried rice, no shrimp,
not spicy, not sour.

171
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,080
Not eating.

172
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,559
Can we do that again? I missed it.

173
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:14,679
This is what the hotel looked like back in the day.

174
00:11:15,279 --> 00:11:17,600
Beautiful, isn’t it?

175
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,480
Wooow.

176
00:11:27,399 --> 00:11:28,399
Dead silence.

177
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,759
And this is what the hotel looks like now.

178
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,799
As you all know

179
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,799
this was the very first hotel in the Double P Group.

180
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:41,840
Then there was the fire twenty years ago...
Such a shame, really.

181
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,679
- So we have no choice but to.
- Let’s just get to the point.

182
00:11:44,879 --> 00:11:45,879
You don’t need the recap.

183
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,798
Everyone already knows what happened

184
00:11:48,799 --> 00:11:50,240
I don’t.

185
00:11:55,159 --> 00:11:58,759
The current owner got back
to us and wants to sell.

186
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,159
So I thought...

187
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,200
a beautiful hotel like this...

188
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:07,000
we should buy it back, don’t you think?

189
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:11,840
I want to bring it back
as our Group’s new boutique hotel.

190
00:12:12,519 --> 00:12:14,679
You just want your dad’s hotel back, don’t you?

191
00:12:16,399 --> 00:12:18,519
- But will it even be worth it?”
- Exactly

192
00:12:18,799 --> 00:12:20,840
I do understand where you’re coming from, Pee

193
00:12:21,279 --> 00:12:22,919
but this location...

194
00:12:23,559 --> 00:12:26,759
the view just can’t compete
with most luxury hotels.

195
00:12:27,279 --> 00:12:29,240
If we’re going to renovate it

196
00:12:29,399 --> 00:12:31,759
we’re looking at hundreds of millions more.

197
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,159
Rapee, have you discussed this with your mother?

198
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,440
I understand that very well.

199
00:12:41,039 --> 00:12:44,279
Right now, I’m still not the company president.

200
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,758
Because the moment I am,

201
00:12:46,759 --> 00:12:49,439
I won’t have to sit here discussing it
with everyone like this. Right?

202
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,799
Mr. Rapee... Ms. Ramphueng...

203
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,240
Hey!

204
00:13:22,759 --> 00:13:23,840
Shit.

205
00:13:24,399 --> 00:13:25,559
The internet froze.

206
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,600
I was this close to taking down TT.

207
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,480
Mine froze too, bro.

208
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,039
Was it a power drop or what?

209
00:13:34,159 --> 00:13:35,440
I got disconnected too.

210
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:37,799
Bii, Bii, did you do something?

211
00:13:38,519 --> 00:13:39,559
I didn’t

212
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:42,119
I definitely did not think the internet plug
and the oven plug were the same one

213
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,599
I didn’t do anything.

214
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,600
I really didn’t.

215
00:13:44,601 --> 00:13:46,039
Fuck, fuck, fuck.

216
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,720
- Hey!
- Hey!

217
00:13:47,759 --> 00:13:49,159
Hey, what’s wrong with you?

218
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,399
- We barely lost.
- Yeah.

219
00:13:51,799 --> 00:13:53,278
You’re way too worked up.

220
00:13:53,279 --> 00:13:54,639
Got something on your mind?

221
00:13:58,080 --> 00:14:01,000
My mom wants me to meet with the board.

222
00:14:01,519 --> 00:14:03,239
I don’t want to go.

223
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,678
I don’t even know how to say no.

224
00:14:05,679 --> 00:14:07,440
That’s easy, bro. Just go.

225
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:11,518
But when you’re on the date,
just act like an asshole.

226
00:14:11,519 --> 00:14:12,959
They’ll leave on their own.

227
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,080
- Is that seriously your advice?
- Yep.

228
00:14:16,039 --> 00:14:18,279
Act like an asshole.

229
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:55,679
What are you laughing at? I’m sick.

230
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,759
Mom, is something wrong?

231
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,879
If I weren’t so sick I could barely get up,

232
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,440
you probably wouldn’t have come
to see me, would you?

233
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,559
No, Mom

234
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,200
I got here as fast as I could

235
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,518
I hit a motorbike
in the middle of an intersection.

236
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,999
They went down,
and I have no idea how they’re doing.

237
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,840
- Huh?
- You’re all better now?

238
00:15:25,919 --> 00:15:27,439
You were joking just now, weren’t you?

239
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,639
So you’re not actually sick, right, Mom?

240
00:15:32,399 --> 00:15:37,479
I went to see the doctor.
I haven’t been feeling well today.

241
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,440
And the doctor told me...

242
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,080
told me I have cancer.

243
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,240
Uh-huh.

244
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:51,240
Oh, honestly, this child of mine
how can you be so cold?

245
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,879
Cold how, Mom?

246
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:55,120
Just look at yourself.
Where do you look sick?

247
00:15:55,279 --> 00:15:57,038
And what earrings are those, huh?

248
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:59,279
What kind of sick person
wears diamond earrings that big?

249
00:16:00,639 --> 00:16:02,080
Seriously, Mom

250
00:16:02,679 --> 00:16:05,440
what do you really want from me today?

251
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
- I want a grandchild.
- I don’t even have a wife.

252
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:10,159
- Then go find one.
- I just don’t want to yet.

253
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,600
What is it with you?

254
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:15,000
People your age
are already married with kids

255
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,480
I don’t even know when I’m going to die.

256
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:21,759
Am I really going to die
before I ever see my grandchild?

257
00:16:29,039 --> 00:16:31,440
And did you discuss this
with your mother first?

258
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:38,080
Mom, I’ll get married for you if I have to.

259
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,879
Really?

260
00:16:42,879 --> 00:16:44,600
Why do you change your mind so easily?

261
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,080
But.

262
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:47,720
But what?

263
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:52,158
But you have to give me
the company president position first.

264
00:16:52,159 --> 00:16:53,480
Okay?

265
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,518
Once you’re gone,
that position is mine anyway.

266
00:16:58,519 --> 00:16:59,919
There’s no need to rush.

267
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,360
Mom.

268
00:17:03,039 --> 00:17:06,279
I want to buy Dad’s old hotel and renovate it.

269
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:08,720
But the board won’t approve it.

270
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:13,799
Pee, are you still not over this?

271
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:27,440
Go, go! Whoever gets there first joins the new game.

272
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:29,719
Come on, come on!
First one there wins! First one there wins!

273
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,720
Go on.

274
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,440
Where’s the sound coming from?

275
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,440
Right here.

276
00:17:44,119 --> 00:17:46,119
If it weren’t for that hotel back then,

277
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,640
we wouldn’t have this family today, Mom.

278
00:17:55,559 --> 00:17:57,519
If you promise to get married,

279
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,599
I’ll give it to you.

280
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,159
So the second I get married,
you’ll hand it over?

281
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,160
Mm-hmm.

282
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,920
I don’t know your name,

283
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,359
but marry me.

284
00:18:16,799 --> 00:18:17,799
I will.

285
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,519
Oh no, no.

286
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,160
Not this one.

287
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:24,200
I’ve already found someone suitable for you.

288
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:25,640
Come here.

289
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:26,880
Ow.

290
00:18:27,279 --> 00:18:29,799
Do you remember Nong Noppakao?

291
00:18:32,519 --> 00:18:34,160
Noppakao?

292
00:18:50,599 --> 00:18:52,279
Please, come in.

293
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,920
You’re even wearing a suit.

294
00:19:05,039 --> 00:19:06,680
Hello, Ms. Noppakao.

295
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,640
Hello, P’Rapee.

296
00:19:35,079 --> 00:19:37,000
The reason I asked you here today is...

297
00:19:48,759 --> 00:19:50,199
The reason I asked you here today...

298
00:19:50,839 --> 00:19:53,200
My mom told me you’re interested in me.

299
00:19:55,079 --> 00:19:56,079
What?

300
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,160
That’s not it.

301
00:19:59,559 --> 00:20:01,319
P’Pee, could you explain that a little more?

302
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,160
My mom said,

303
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:07,799
please, she said
the girl was interested in you.

304
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:10,640
Interested in me?

305
00:20:11,359 --> 00:20:13,599
Then why hasn’t she added me yet, Mom?

306
00:20:14,039 --> 00:20:15,799
She’s well mannered.

307
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,960
Maybe she’s just shy, son.

308
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,400
Oh, so that’s how it is.

309
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:27,920
Because what your mom told Kao
was something else.

310
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,000
My mom told me that
the moment you saw my profile,

311
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:34,479
you completely lost it.
I’m really proud you’re like that.

312
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:35,480
Thanks for coming.

313
00:20:36,039 --> 00:20:37,799
Bitch.

314
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,480
Sigh.

315
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:54,119
Why does the AC in here feel so cold?

316
00:20:54,599 --> 00:20:57,160
P’Pee, could you turn it up a bit?

317
00:21:02,559 --> 00:21:04,480
Now that P’Pee’s met Kao today,

318
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,480
what do you think of me?

319
00:21:07,559 --> 00:21:08,599
Hmm.

320
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:11,039
You’ll do.

321
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,240
The hell? Even with my foot
in your face, I’d still ‘do’?

322
00:21:17,799 --> 00:21:19,399
I want to talk to you about marriage.

323
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:20,480
Marriage?

324
00:21:23,319 --> 00:21:26,440
What do you mean?
We just met today, P’Pee.

325
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:29,880
And my mom didn’t say
anything about marriage.

326
00:21:30,359 --> 00:21:32,000
What your parents think doesn’t matter.

327
00:21:33,759 --> 00:21:35,720
Oh?

328
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,759
Not even caring about my mom now, huh?

329
00:21:39,279 --> 00:21:41,680
I just want you to know I’m very rich.

330
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:50,920
P’Pee.

331
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:54,000
I’m cold.

332
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,000
Could you turn the AC up a little more?

333
00:22:06,799 --> 00:22:07,799
Please, go on.

334
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:12,639
What I mean is,
I think the two of us should.

335
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,240
The food here looks so good.

336
00:22:16,039 --> 00:22:17,039
Order it, order it

337
00:22:17,279 --> 00:22:19,919
I understand this is
all happening too fast for you.

338
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:22,039
Holy shit, this is crazy expensive.

339
00:22:22,519 --> 00:22:24,079
How are they even selling this?

340
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,400
Two, please.

341
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,200
This is a very important matter.

342
00:22:32,359 --> 00:22:35,039
So I want us to get fake-married.

343
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,960
What do you mean, P’Pee? Kao’s confused.

344
00:22:40,279 --> 00:22:43,119
Even if I explained it,
you probably wouldn’t understand.

345
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,136
I’ll understand even less if you don’t explain.

346
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:46,319
Alright, then...

347
00:22:46,759 --> 00:22:49,519
This marriage is about my work.

348
00:22:49,839 --> 00:22:51,440
And I need this sorted out fast.

349
00:22:52,559 --> 00:22:55,240
I need you to marry me for one year.

350
00:22:55,559 --> 00:22:57,319
Be my fake wife.

351
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,879
Once the year’s up, we get divorced

352
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,640
and go our separate ways. Sound good?

353
00:23:08,039 --> 00:23:09,039
Five million.

354
00:23:10,599 --> 00:23:12,079
One year. Five million.

355
00:23:12,799 --> 00:23:13,839
Interested?

356
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,800
Kao’s just going to the restroom for a second.

357
00:23:23,039 --> 00:23:24,039
Ten million.

358
00:23:28,079 --> 00:23:29,400
I’ll just be a second.

359
00:23:29,559 --> 00:23:31,599
I’ll be right back,
and then we can keep talking.

360
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:50,559
You’re leaving already?

361
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,960
Oh, yes. I’m leaving now.

362
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,200
Oh, bye.

363
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,240
Bye.

364
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:09,558
Your bride-to-be ditched you the other day
and left you sitting there waiting.

365
00:24:09,559 --> 00:24:10,799
Bet that scared you off, huh?

366
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:13,160
How could I be scared off?

367
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:16,039
If I were, I’d never become president.

368
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,160
Mom.

369
00:24:20,519 --> 00:24:21,959
- Well done, my niece.
- Well done, sweetheart.

370
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:22,960
Again.

371
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:25,079
Yeah, kick it. Kick it!

372
00:24:25,279 --> 00:24:26,399
Seriously,

373
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:28,480
you’d go that far trade marriage for this?

374
00:24:31,799 --> 00:24:33,119
You ever been married?

375
00:24:34,079 --> 00:24:35,400
What you’re really scared of

376
00:24:36,079 --> 00:24:37,960
is not becoming president, right?

377
00:24:38,119 --> 00:24:40,039
An arranged marriage is bad enough already.

378
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:41,759
And then you throw money at her too?

379
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,640
If it were me, I wouldn’t marry you either.

380
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,880
Yeah, yeah, I get it. You’re rich.

381
00:24:46,039 --> 00:24:47,359
You don’t have to flaunt it.

382
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,160
Mom.

383
00:24:50,359 --> 00:24:52,039
Good job, sweetheart.

384
00:24:52,799 --> 00:24:54,559
That’s amazing, Rial.

385
00:24:57,559 --> 00:25:01,200
So... what do I do now?

386
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:05,559
When it comes to love,
you’ve got to put your heart on the line.

387
00:25:07,279 --> 00:25:08,759
Mom, help!

388
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:09,720
- Hey!
- Mom!

389
00:25:09,759 --> 00:25:10,640
Oh my god, my child.

390
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:12,240
Let go of my kid.

391
00:25:12,839 --> 00:25:15,279
Sweetheart, Mom’s here!

392
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:18,440
Mom...

393
00:25:24,759 --> 00:25:26,999
Hi, I’m Bas, gamer.

394
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,359
Right now, the WOG Champion League Thailand

395
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:33,160
has twenty-three teams.

396
00:25:34,759 --> 00:25:38,440
But there’s still one spot left for Team Twenty-Four.

397
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:43,920
That team will be decided by a wild-card draw
here at Thailand Comic.

398
00:25:44,119 --> 00:25:49,039
We’re about to find out who Team Twenty-Four will be.

399
00:25:51,079 --> 00:25:52,119
What’re you laughing at?

400
00:25:52,279 --> 00:25:53,839
Yeah, well, we’ll find out in a second.

401
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:56,000
You guys ready?

402
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,200
Ready!

403
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,359
Shit.

404
00:26:05,559 --> 00:26:06,720
Damn.

405
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:08,960
So nobody got anything at all?

406
00:26:09,079 --> 00:26:11,880
Shit, this outfit’s hot as hell
And we didn’t win a damn thing.

407
00:26:12,519 --> 00:26:15,000
Are we really never gonna
make it as pro players in this life?

408
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:19,119
Hey, Kao.

409
00:26:19,359 --> 00:26:20,839
So what happened yesterday

410
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:22,719
with that arranged-marriage
thing your mom set up?

411
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:25,519
What was his name again?
Mr. Rapee of Double P Group.

412
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:28,480
Man, he was so, so freaking weird.

413
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:32,119
What kind of asshole offers me five million just to marry him?

414
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:33,759
Five million?

415
00:26:34,559 --> 00:26:35,559
Yeah.

416
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:38,400
But not for real, okay? Like, fake marriage.

417
00:26:38,559 --> 00:26:40,919
He’d pay me five million to do it for one year.

418
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:41,960
What for?

419
00:26:42,480 --> 00:26:43,559
No idea.

420
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:45,279
His logic’s seriously messed up

421
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:48,559
I know.
I think that guy probably wants to, like...

422
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:51,319
Mm-hmm

423
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:52,720
totally do it with you for sure.

424
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,400
What the hell are you talking about?

425
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:57,240
Kao,

426
00:26:57,519 --> 00:27:02,240
that five million could totally
be seed money for our team.

427
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:03,240
Yeah.

428
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:04,400
Shit.

429
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,759
You’ve got a point.

430
00:27:06,519 --> 00:27:08,839
But do you really have to go that far?

431
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:12,720
This tournament...

432
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,559
it’s our last shot

433
00:27:15,359 --> 00:27:16,960
at becoming pro players.

434
00:27:21,319 --> 00:27:23,920
But fuck, we couldn’t even get the wildcard.

435
00:27:24,599 --> 00:27:25,599
Damn it.

436
00:27:26,559 --> 00:27:29,839
Is this really as far as our dream goes?

437
00:27:30,039 --> 00:27:31,039
Damn it.

438
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:40,840
So, how’d it go, sweetheart?

439
00:27:41,359 --> 00:27:42,839
You met Rapee the other day.

440
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,680
You still haven’t told us about it.

441
00:27:46,359 --> 00:27:47,599
So what’s the verdict?

442
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,000
The verdict on what?

443
00:27:50,359 --> 00:27:53,039
Hey, Dad what happened to your eye?

444
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,680
A patient’s family member punched me.

445
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,000
Well, not the patient.

446
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,480
It was the patient’s son.

447
00:27:57,680 --> 00:27:58,680
My fault, really.

448
00:27:58,681 --> 00:28:00,359
I tripped over his mother’s oxygen tube.

449
00:28:01,519 --> 00:28:03,039
So, are you going to marry him or not?

450
00:28:04,319 --> 00:28:06,359
What are you so startled for? Still not used to it?

451
00:28:07,319 --> 00:28:10,279
So? You met him was he handsome enough for you?

452
00:28:10,559 --> 00:28:11,559
Come on, tell us.

453
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:17,078
Let’s talk about it later, Mom.

454
00:28:17,079 --> 00:28:18,079
- Hey.
- Wait.

455
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,640
Running off again? Come out and talk first.

456
00:28:24,039 --> 00:28:25,400
I’ll go open it.

457
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,640
Come out and talk first.

458
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:40,920
Mom, I told you, can we talk another day?

459
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:42,160
Fine.

460
00:28:46,119 --> 00:28:47,480
He came all the way here?

461
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:50,920
Hi, P’Pee.

462
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,799
Uh, come in first.

463
00:28:54,559 --> 00:28:55,599
Hey, hold on.

464
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:58,320
With that horny look on your face,
is that really a good idea?

465
00:28:58,559 --> 00:29:00,559
It’s okay. We can talk right here

466
00:29:00,759 --> 00:29:03,159
I just... wanted to talk to you for a second.

467
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:04,160
Mm.

468
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:05,839
I brought this for you.

469
00:29:11,359 --> 00:29:12,359
It’s just...

470
00:29:13,079 --> 00:29:14,599
I want to apologize.

471
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:18,040
For throwing money in your face that day.

472
00:29:20,559 --> 00:29:22,598
For disrespecting you

473
00:29:22,599 --> 00:29:25,160
and maybe treating you badly.

474
00:29:25,319 --> 00:29:26,599
I’m really sorry.

475
00:29:28,119 --> 00:29:29,519
It’s okay.

476
00:29:33,119 --> 00:29:34,200
Um, P’Pee...

477
00:29:36,759 --> 00:29:38,559
Kao wants to apologize too.

478
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,640
For pointing my foot at your face that day.

479
00:29:45,160 --> 00:29:46,519
For disrespecting you.

480
00:29:48,279 --> 00:29:49,279
It’s really okay.

481
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:51,799
Because if I were you,

482
00:29:52,559 --> 00:29:54,240
I would’ve done the same.

483
00:29:57,519 --> 00:29:59,240
- See you around.
- Okay.

484
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:23,279
What are you two staring at?

485
00:31:01,359 --> 00:31:02,559
Hello, Kao?

486
00:31:03,039 --> 00:31:04,079
Kao?

487
00:31:05,039 --> 00:31:06,960
Bii, help me out here. Okay.

488
00:31:07,759 --> 00:31:08,839
Thanks.

489
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:13,759
What is it?

490
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:15,839
Hey, I’ve got something to tell you.

491
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:17,240
Dude, I’m home.

492
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:19,640
I got the email.

493
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,558
The one about culinary school.

494
00:31:21,559 --> 00:31:23,119
I leave in six months.

495
00:31:23,319 --> 00:31:24,319
Shit.

496
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:28,400
Whoa, future Chef Fai in the making or what?

497
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:29,999
I’m going to pastry school,

498
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:31,480
not learning how to make omelets.

499
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:37,720
Whatever, it still means
you’re one step closer to your dream.

500
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:41,758
Hah. And when is Noppakao of Rungtawan Witthaya

501
00:31:41,759 --> 00:31:43,960
going to get any closer to her own dream?

502
00:31:45,839 --> 00:31:46,960
Sigh.

503
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:49,759
Hey...

504
00:31:50,079 --> 00:31:52,200
Do you still want to be a pro player?

505
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:55,960
Yeah.

506
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,279
If you still want it.

507
00:31:58,799 --> 00:32:00,680
I might have a way to help.

508
00:32:02,279 --> 00:32:03,279
How?

509
00:32:07,039 --> 00:32:08,640
That pro league slot

510
00:32:08,799 --> 00:32:10,200
we missed this year...

511
00:32:10,559 --> 00:32:13,799
I heard there’s a team called Ultra Pig

512
00:32:14,519 --> 00:32:17,359
that’s willing to sell their slot.

513
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:21,079
The owner’s name is Auntie Jeung.

514
00:32:22,039 --> 00:32:23,319
And the price is.

515
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:25,440
Five hundred thousand.

516
00:32:25,839 --> 00:32:27,079
Can I get it for five thousand?

517
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:28,319
Ha!

518
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:30,719
A slot in a gaming league,

519
